  "body": "## What changed\n\n`AGENTS.md` now holds the rules only. It is written in ASD-STE100. The procedures that one task uses are in five new skills. A table at the top of `AGENTS.md` names the skill for each task.\n\n| File | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `AGENTS.md` | 1240 lines, 81,389 bytes | 697 lines, 40,400 bytes |\n\nEach agent loads `AGENTS.md` in each session. The five skills (639 lines) load only when an agent does that task.\n\n## Where each moved section is now\n\n| Old section of `AGENTS.md` | New place |\n|---|---|\n| Gate flags, quick selection, `SLOW_BINARIES`, heavy-lane steps, narrow ladder, sccache, `VisualRunner`, local batch gate | `.claude/skills/gate/SKILL.md` |\n| Cut runner installation, post-merge gate details, PR test runner details, billed minutes | `.claude/skills/runners/SKILL.md` |\n| Cut steps 1 to 5, start condition, changelog row format | `.claude/skills/release-cut/SKILL.md` |\n| Fork sync at cut tags, process-file sync | `.claude/skills/fork-sync/SKILL.md` |\n| Claim mirror, stale release, withdrawal, maintenance sweep, `needs-research` steps | `.claude/skills/issue-claims/SKILL.md` |\n| PR rules from three sections | One section, \"Pull Request Law\", in `AGENTS.md` |\n\n`docs/decisions/1829-agents-md-compress.md` has the full table, the dropped text and the options that were not used.\n\n## What stays\n\n- The rule of each moved section stays in `AGENTS.md`, with a pointer to the skill.\n- Each rule name that a skill, an agent, a workflow or a code comment cites is still a bold name or a heading. A script checked this for 41 names.\n- Clean-Room Protocol, Prime Directive, Everything Is a Command, Assets, Dependencies and Code shape keep all their rules.\n\n## What was dropped\n\n- The dated quotations of the maintainer and the \"superseded since\" notes. They are in the git history (`git log -p -- AGENTS.md`).\n- The \"Was\" column of the priority table.\n\n## For the maintainer to check\n\nThese rules have new wording. The meaning must be the same:\n\n- \"Every PR opens as a draft\": the merge-time refresh classes.\n- \"Only collaborators' reviews count\": the disagreement case.\n- \"A claim must be live\".\n- The four cut rules in \"A cut goes PR review -> merge to main -> tag\".\n\nThe issue asked for a much shorter file. The result is half the size, not a quarter: a shorter file loses rules.\n\n## How tested\n\n- Docs only. No build and no test ran.\n- A script searched `AGENTS.md` for each cited rule name. All are there.\n- The existing skills and agents are not changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No agent has worked an issue, a merge batch or a cut with the new files.\n- A fork has not pulled the new skills.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nFixes #1829\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
